       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Sertraline 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Doses that high raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding effects. I don't know of evidence that doses above 200 mg work better.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n\n1. **A typo or unit slip.** For example, you may have meant 40 mg or 200 mg. I can enter whichever dose you confirm. The usual start is 50 mg once daily, and it is titrated up to a maximum of 200 mg/day.\n2. **A deliberate above-maximum dose.** If so, please confirm that, and I'll enter it with a note saying it exceeds the labeled maximum and was intentionally prescribed. You may also want to check for interacting serotonergic or QT-prolonging drugs and consider an ECG.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
